[Key Analytical Discovery]:
  Notice that Port FastEthernet0/4 on Switch-B has dynamically learned MULTIPLE
  MAC addresses (Host-A1, Host-A2, and Host-A3)!
  Because Hub-A multiplexes all traffic from LAN-A onto that single uplink cable,
  every frame from LAN-A arrives at Switch-B via port Fa0/4.
  This proves switches support multi-MAC port associations when connected to hubs.
